<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <!-- CarPlay. Uncomment both lines below once the App ID carries the
       capability, and everything else is already in place: the scene is
       declared in Info.plist, the delegate is built, and the app is started
       from its app delegate so a car reaching a never-foregrounded app finds a
       working library.

       It is commented out rather than present because an entitlement the App ID
       does not carry does not merely warn — it fails the archive outright:

           error: Entitlement com.apple.developer.carplay-audio not found and
           could not be included in profile.

       Verified against the account on 2026-08-31: the App ID
       com.benjaminissa.issareader (<bundle id record>) carries only APP_GROUPS and
       IN_APP_PURCHASE, and its active App Store profile has no carplay-audio
       entitlement. Apple granting the entitlement to the account is the first
       half; the App ID has to be given it too.

       No API can do that second half. CarPlay is an "Additional Capability" in
       the Developer portal, and App Store Connect's own CapabilityType
       enumeration has no CarPlay value at all — so neither `xcodebuild
       -allowProvisioningUpdates` nor the API can register it. It is:

           Certificates, Identifiers & Profiles -> Identifiers ->
           com.benjaminissa.issareader -> Additional Capabilities -> CarPlay

       After ticking it, uncomment, and the next archive regenerates the profile
       with the entitlement in it.

  <key>com.apple.developer.carplay-audio</key>
  <true/>
  -->
  <key>com.apple.security.application-groups</key>
  <array>
    <string>group.com.benjaminissa.issareader</string>
  </array>
</dict>
</plist>
